  "summary_en": "Vermont's Automated Vehicle Testing Act (23 V.S.A. ch. 41) defines automated driving terms and requires a Traffic Committee permit before automated vehicles are tested on public highways, with operator, insurance, crash reporting, and permit revocation requirements.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Testing on public highways requires Traffic Committee permit defining the operational design domain, after public hearing.",
   "Municipalities may preapprove or revoke testing on Class 2-4 town highways.",
   "A trained operator must sit in the driver's seat, ready to take manual control.",
   "Testers must carry at least $5 million liability insurance, self-insurance, or surety bond.",
   "Crashes must be reported within 72 hours; permits may be voided, suspended or revoked; violations carry up to $1,000 penalty."
  ],
